            "treatment.7",
            "treatment.8",
            "treatment.9"
          ],
          "text": "Multi-organ support: intubated and ventilated, noradrenaline, and CVVH for AKI.\n\nSurgical: four debridements on days 0, 2, 5 and 9, followed by washout, delayed closure and VAC dressing. Wound healing by secondary intention with district nurse and tissue viability involvement.\n\nAntimicrobial therapy: long course IV piperacillin-tazobactam, then tailored to benzylpenicillin and clindamycin per microbiology advice.\n\nRespiratory: prone positioning x2 for ARDS.\n\nLine sepsis on day 14 managed with line changes.\n\nNutrition via nasogastric tube, progressing to improving oral intake.\n\nClinical course: renal function recovered; off CVVH day 16; extubated day 18; stepped down to ward day 24.\n\nProlonged rehabilitation and physiotherapy throughout admission.",
