            "treatment.7",
            "treatment.8",
            "treatment.9"
          ],
          "text": "Wound and tissue cultures grew Group A Streptococcus and anaerobes. She required full multi-organ support including intubation and ventilation, noradrenaline, and CVVH for AKI. She underwent four surgical debridements (days 0, 2, 5 and 9), washout, delayed closure and VAC dressing, with ongoing wound healing by secondary intention under district nurse and tissue viability review. Antimicrobials were commenced as IV piperacillin-tazobactam and rationalised to benzylpenicillin and clindamycin per microbiology advice. She was proned twice for ARDS. Line sepsis on day 14 was managed with line changes. Nutrition was initially via nasogastric tube, progressing to oral intake. Renal function recovered and CVVH was discontinued on day 16; she was extubated on day 18 and stepped down to the ward on day 24. She received prolonged rehabilitation and physiotherapy throughout.",
